\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1.\cf0  Lord Jesus you came into
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 this world as a human being
\par You subjected to the law
\par and suffered under its rule.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. We descendants of Adam
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 are all offending sinners
\par infested by sin throughout
\par right from our own mother's womb.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. You the new Adam has come
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 embracing all of our guilt
\par taking all the past judgment
\par to bring us a new sovereign
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0 
\par \pard\fi-180\li315\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4.  We are the guilty sinners
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0  You are the clean lamb of God
\par  Adam's death was passed to us
\par   You are the only Saviour.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-180\li315\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5.  The old birth was not so clean
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0  But you have come to cleanse us
\par  and in your new covenant
\par \pard        we have become God's children.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

